// Regression test for Bug 2 (replace_program_is_noop()'s function-ACCESS-
// flags comparison, src/packages/core/replace_program.cc). Fixtures:
// /clone/replace_program/replace_bug2_private_base (a PRIVATE function),
// /clone/replace_program/replace_bug2_wrapper (the redundant self-target boilerplate
// inheriting it).
//
// This LPC-level test can only observe that a swap got PENDING -- see
// replace_program_noop_globals.lpc's comment for why (no gametick elapses
// mid-suite). Proving the actual BEHAVIORAL difference (self-call-other
// permission genuinely differs pre- vs. post-swap) needs forcing the
// deferred sweep synchronously; see
// ReplaceProgramBug2PrivateFlagsAffectSelfCallPermission in
// src/tests/test_lpc.cc.
void do_tests() {
  object ob = clone_object("/clone/replace_program/replace_bug2_wrapper");
  // A pending swap must exist: replace_program_is_noop() must correctly
  // see the DECL_PRIVATE (base's own slot) vs. DECL_HIDDEN (wrapper's own
  // copy) mismatch on secret() and refuse the no-op fast path.
  ASSERT(ob->try_bind());
  destruct(ob);
}
